  "goodToKnow": "Der Zeichner (die Zeichnerin) is a draughtsman, illustrator or cartoonist: technischer Zeichner (a recognised training occupation), Comiczeichner, Karikaturist. Wilhelm Busch, creator of Max und Moritz (1865), is seen as a forefather of comics. Zeichnen means to draw, and die Zeichnung is a drawing. Der Zeichentrickfilm is an animated cartoon. Plural: die Zeichner."
